# Feature work happens in a worktree under here — the root manual's first hard
# rule — and the manual also says the directory stays out of version control.
# This file is the half of that claim git can enforce: without it, `git add -A`
# in the root checkout stages a live worktree as an embedded repository, and
# git's own warning is the only thing that says so.
worktree/

# The kit traces its own decisions under here (scripts/trace.kit.config.sh,
# the kit's ADR-0008). The trace is local by design — findings, reasons and token counts
# in plain text — and the kit never pushes it; a gitignored directory is also
# invisible to the docs gate's placeholder scan, which is the point.
.trace/

# The retrospective's reports — /retro writes `.retro/<YYYY>/<MM>/retro-<stamp>.md`
# and its CSV export here, at the root checkout, resolved through git's common
# directory the way the trace directory above is. A report quotes the trace
# (reasons, comment bodies, costs), so it is local for the same reason the
# trace is, and never pushed.
.retro/
